	On the subject of partially-eaten food, a helpful spoiler:

If you are weak (or hungry, it doesn't matter, but why eat when you don't
need to?) and start to eat a food ration, but get interrupted by a monster,
you will still fill up as if you ate the whole ration.  So now you're no
longer hungry but have a partially-eaten food ration.  Next time you need to
eat, eat the partial ration, which should function just like a normal ration.
	Interrupting your eating of a food ration makes it seem as if you
ate a full ration, then later on ate another full ration.  In other words,
it appears that each time you just snack on a ration you still get the full
nutritional benefits.
